        <item>
            <title>1.14.0</title>
            <pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:46:39 +0530</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>243</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.14.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<ul>
  <li>Homebrew updates show on Updates as soon as Homebrew knows them: when Homebrew already has a newer version of an app it installed, Updates offers it straight away, and every check now asks for Homebrew&#x27;s latest list, not only Check Now.</li>
  <li>Settings › Sources › Connections lists every server Keel has reached, what for, how many apps, and the country, with an all-time count and Export as CSV. It stays on your Mac; countries come from a table inside Keel.</li>
  <li>Claude: when Claude&#x27;s own updater has a new version ready, its row says so with a Restart Claude button. Otherwise Keel waits two days before offering a new Claude version, while Anthropic rolls it out.</li>
  <li>After you start an update, an app Keel quit comes back in front with its window, and the row says &quot;reopened&quot; only once it really did (otherwise &quot;didn&#x27;t come back&quot;, with Open).</li>
  <li>Not Covered apps get Request Coverage, ready for Keel&#x27;s own request service; until it&#x27;s switched on, the button opens GitHub as before.</li>
  <li>Clearer messages when this Mac can&#x27;t look up a download server (check your VPN, DNS filter or firewall app), and when a server still hands out the previous version (Keel tries again at the next check).</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
